      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SOLID Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What SOLID Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==SOLID== = five class-design rules for easy-to-change code",
                "{blue:SRP}, {green:OCP}, {purple:LSP}, {orange:ISP}, {red:DIP}",
                "Core goal: one requirement change touches ==one place==",
                "Not a ripple across many classes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Smell to Principle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Smell",
                "Principle"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Giant class",
                  "==SRP=="
                ],
                [
                  "Growing if/else on type",
                  "==OCP=="
                ],
                [
                  "Subclass that throws",
                  "==LSP=="
                ],
                [
                  "Unused methods",
                  "==ISP=="
                ],
                [
                  "`new` of concrete deps",
                  "==DIP=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Judgment",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Guidelines for managing change, **not laws**",
                "Apply when a ==real change pressure== appears"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "No change pressure, no refactor. Do not pre-split for imagined futures."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why SOLID?** Keeps change local and cheap",
                "**Smell to principle?** Giant class SRP, type if/else OCP, throwing subclass LSP, unused methods ISP, `new` deps DIP",
                "**Overkill when?** Stable code, one type, no second reason to change"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Single Responsibility and Open/Closed",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Single Responsibility and Open/Closed",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Single Responsibility",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One reason to change== = one **actor** owns the class",
                "{red:Bad}: `Invoice` has `calculateTotal()`, `saveToDb()`, `printPdf()`",
                "Tax, DB and layout changes all edit one class"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "Owns",
                "Changes with"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Invoice`",
                  "data, totals",
                  "tax rules"
                ],
                [
                  "`InvoiceRepository`",
                  "persistence",
                  "DB"
                ],
                [
                  "`InvoicePrinter`",
                  "output",
                  "layout"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Open/Closed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Open to extension, closed to modification==",
                "Add behavior by adding code, not editing tested code",
                "{red:Bad}: `area(shape)` uses if/elif on type; every new shape edits it",
                "{green:Fix}: `Shape` interface with `area()`; each shape implements it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod",
                "class Shape(ABC):",
                "    @abstractmethod",
                "    def area(self): ...",
                "class Circle(Shape):",
                "    def area(self): return 3.14 * self.r ** 2"
              ],
              "note": "new shape = new class, no edits"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Premature OCP",
              "text": "Wait for the ==third== variant (rule of three)."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Reason to change?** One actor's requirement: tax, DB, layout",
                "**OCP vs SRP?** OCP extends without editing; SRP gives one owner",
                "**OCP pattern?** Polymorphism / Strategy",
                "**Premature when?** One type, no new types expected"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Liskov Substitution Principle",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Liskov Substitution Principle",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==LSP==: a subtype works wherever its base type is expected",
                "No stronger {red:preconditions} (what callers must supply)",
                "No weaker {red:postconditions} (what callers get back)",
                "Keep every base ==invariant=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Violations",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Square` setters change both sides, so a `Rectangle` caller gets the wrong area",
                "`Penguin.fly()` throws: any caller holding a Penguin as a Bird crashes"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "r = Square()  # extends Rect",
                "r.set_width(5)",
                "r.set_height(4)",
                "r.area()  # caller expects 20, gets 16"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fix: Model Behavior",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Model",
                "Base",
                "Implementers"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Birds",
                  "`Flyer.fly()`",
                  "Sparrow; Penguin is only a Bird"
                ],
                [
                  "Shapes",
                  "`Shape.area()`",
                  "Rectangle, Square (independent)"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Detect a break?** An override throws, or a base caller's expectation fails",
                "**Why Square fails?** It breaks Rect's invariant: width and height are independent",
                "**Precondition?** What callers must supply. **Postcondition**: what the method guarantees"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Interface Segregation and Dependency Inversion",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Interface Segregation and Dependency Inversion",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Interface Segregation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ISP==: no client forced to depend on methods it does not use",
                "Prefer many small **role interfaces**",
                "{red:Violation}: `Worker` has `work()` and `eat()`",
                "`Robot` must no-op or throw in `eat()`",
                "{green:Fix}: split into `Workable` and `Eatable`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dependency Inversion",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==DIP==: high-level modules depend on **abstractions**",
                "Both high and low level depend on the interface",
                "{red:Violation}: `OrderService` runs `self.db = MySQLDatabase()`",
                "Cannot test or swap it",
                "{green:Fix}: `Database` interface, injected via constructor"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class OrderService:",
                "    def __init__(self, db: Database):",
                "        self.db = db",
                "svc = OrderService(FakeDatabase())"
              ],
              "note": "tests pass a fake"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Terms Not to Mix Up",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Term",
                "What it is"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "DIP",
                  "==principle=="
                ],
                [
                  "Dependency injection",
                  "**technique**"
                ],
                [
                  "IoC container",
                  "tool"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**ISP vs SRP?** ISP: client's view of an interface; SRP: one reason to change",
                "**DIP vs DI?** Principle vs the technique that applies it",
                "**DIP and unit tests?** Inject a fake, no real DB"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common SOLID Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common SOLID Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Over-Applying SOLID",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Over-splitting==: one-method classes hide the flow; split only on a **real second reason to change**",
                "One interface per class, one implementation, no test seam: noise, not {red:DIP}",
                "Type switch in one place, no new types expected: ==leave it== (rule of three)"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inheritance vs Composition",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Inherit for reuse",
                "Compose"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Link",
                  "is-a by convenience",
                  "has-a, delegates"
                ],
                [
                  "LSP",
                  "{red:overrides break callers}",
                  "{green:nothing to override}"
                ],
                [
                  "Fix",
                  "",
                  "independent `Shape` types"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Spot in Review",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Smell",
                "Principle",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fat `Manager` / `Util` class",
                  "SRP",
                  "split by actor"
                ],
                [
                  "`new Concrete()` in constructor",
                  "DIP",
                  "inject interface"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Over-apply SOLID?** Yes: no change pressure means only extra indirection",
                "**Composition vs inheritance for LSP?** Composition has no override to break",
                "**Spot SRP issues?** Manager/Util names, edits from several teams"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule",
              "text": "Split on ==real change pressure==, not on principle names."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SOLID Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SOLID Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Smell and Fix",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Rule",
                "Smell",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**S**RP",
                  "DB + logic + output in one class",
                  "Split responsibilities"
                ],
                [
                  "**O**CP",
                  "if/elif on type",
                  "Polymorphism or Strategy"
                ],
                [
                  "**L**SP",
                  "Override throws or changes semantics",
                  "Composition, smaller interfaces"
                ],
                [
                  "**I**SP",
                  "Empty or throwing methods",
                  "Split the interface"
                ],
                [
                  "**D**IP",
                  "`new Concrete()` in a service",
                  "Constructor injection"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rules to Remember",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "SRP: ==one reason== to change = one actor",
                "OCP: extend by adding code, not editing",
                "LSP: keep the base ==contract==",
                "ISP: small ==role interfaces==",
                "DIP is the principle, ==DI== the technique"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class OrderService:",
                "    def __init__(self, db: Database):",
                "        self.db = db  # injected"
              ],
              "note": "DIP fix: inject, never MySQLDatabase()"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Don't over-apply",
              "text": "Split only on a real second reason to change; one-impl interfaces are noise."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Recite:** giant class, if/elif, throwing override, empty method, `new`",
                "**Hardest?** ==LSP==, its contract is implicit",
                "**Most overlap?** SRP and ISP, both split by role"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
