          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A `Square` extends `Rectangle`. Its setWidth also sets height, and setHeight also sets width. After `r.setWidth(5); r.setHeight(4)` on a Square, what is `r.area()`?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "==16==: the second call resets both sides to 4",
                "The caller expects 20, so Square is not substitutable: an LSP break"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`Penguin extends Bird` and its `fly()` throws. A loop calls `fly()` on every Bird. What breaks, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The loop crashes on the Penguin: an LSP break",
                "Move `fly()` into a `Flyer` interface that only flyers implement"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`OrderService` does `self.db = MySQLDatabase()` in its constructor. Why can't you unit test it, and what fixes it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It creates a concrete dependency, so no fake can be swapped in: a DIP break",
                "Define a `Database` interface and inject it through the constructor"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
